  "security_implications": "All assignments belong to the HMAC core, which computes message authentication codes. sha_message_length_o and sel_msglen directly control the message length and padding selection crucial for HMAC correctness; an error could lead to an incorrect digest that compromises integrity. inc_txcount increments on every valid SHA data transfer; a miscount may corrupt the data stream or cause early termination, potentially leaking internal state. The digest_size_i constraint ensures only supported digest sizes are active; relaxing it could enable a mismatched algorithm path, undermining security properties. No key/secret signals appear, but the surrounding module likely handles them, so correct operation here is a precondition for overall security.",
